#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:1
msgid "Import and manage transactions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:3
msgid ""
"This page covers the ledger's transaction workflow: importing your bank "
"statement, adding any missing transactions by hand, reviewing and "
"correcting them, and checking readiness before a calculation. A line on a"
" bank statement is just a date and an amount - the tax meaning is added "
"later, in classification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:9
msgid ""
"Your bank records are not added automatically. aeat imports only when you"
" run an import command. Tax calculations use the transactions you have "
"saved under the active profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:13
msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:15
msgid "You need:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:17
msgid "a working `aeat` command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:18
msgid ""
"an active taxpayer profile; see [Set up your taxpayer profile](profile-"
"setup.md)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:19
msgid ""
"a master-key passphrase. The tool prompts for it the first time it opens "
"your encrypted storage in a session"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:21
msgid ""
"a bank statement file or directory, unless you are adding transactions by"
" hand"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:22
msgid ""
"for AEAT census-derived home-office ratios, reviewed censo facts; see "
"[Link Modelo 036 census information](censo-update.md)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:25
msgid "Confirm the active profile before you write transaction data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:31
msgid "Statement file format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:33
msgid ""
"A bank CSV uses a semicolon (`;`) separator and comma decimals. The first"
" line is the column header; each later line is one movement:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:42
msgid ""
"The sign of `Importe` carries the direction: a positive amount is income,"
" a negative amount is an expense."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:45
msgid "Preview an import"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:47
msgid ""
"Run a dry run first. A dry run shows what `aeat` would import and saves "
"no rows. Then repeat the command without `--dry-run` to save the rows. "
"The sequence previews the standard quarter's statement, imports it, and "
"confirms one imported row:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:56
msgid ""
"`--provider csv` names the statement format. `--provider auto` asks "
"`aeat` to detect it. The recognized providers are `auto`, `csv`, `ofx`, "
"`qfx`, `xlsx`, `excel`, `n26`, `pdf`, and `pdf-n26`. If detection picks "
"the wrong format, replace `auto` with the exact provider - run `aeat app "
"ledger import --help` or see the [CLI reference](../cli/index.rst) for "
"the current provider list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:62
msgid ""
"If the path does not exist, the command refuses cleanly and names the "
"missing file (`El archivo de origen no existe: ...`); fix the path and "
"run it again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:65
msgid "Save imported rows with diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:67
msgid "Add `--verify` when you want import diagnostics alongside the save:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:73
msgid ""
"If the diagnostic source should point at a different original file, pass "
"it with `--file <original>`. Use `--period` only when you intentionally "
"want to label the import with a fiscal period; leave it out and aeat "
"assigns the period from each transaction's date automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:78
msgid "Add one transaction manually"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:80
msgid ""
"Use `ledger add` when a transaction is missing from imported statements. "
"Required fields are date, amount, direction, and description. Write the "
"amount as a positive figure - the direction carries whether money came in"
" or went out, and the command refuses a negative amount. `OUTGOING` is "
"for expenses; `INCOMING` is for income:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:90
msgid ""
"The third direction, `INTERNAL_TRANSFER`, records money moved between "
"your own accounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:93
msgid "Record tax details on a manual transaction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:95
msgid ""
"`ledger add` accepts the same tax fields you set during classification, "
"so you record a complete transaction in one step. `--amount` is the gross"
" total (taxable base plus IVA), and the tool refuses the row if the base "
"plus IVA does not match the gross to the cent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:104
msgid "Useful optional fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:106
msgid "`--currency` records a non-euro amount; it defaults to `EUR`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:107
msgid "`--counterparty` records who you paid or were paid by."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:108
msgid ""
"`--category-id` assigns the income or expense category. Run `aeat app "
"ledger categories` to list the ids."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:110
msgid ""
"`--taxable-base`, `--iva-rate`, and `--iva-amount` record the IVA "
"breakdown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:111
msgid "`--irpf-category` records the IRPF (personal income tax) category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:112
msgid ""
"`--source-jurisdiction` records the country a movement belongs to, as an "
"ISO two-letter code, which matters for non-resident scopes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:114
msgid "`--notes` adds a short operator note."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:116
msgid ""
"For a part-business, part-personal movement, set `--classification MIXED`"
" and the business share with `--business-pct`, a value from `0` to `1`. "
"For the IVA category, EU member-state, and usage-ratio semantics behind "
"these fields, see [Classify transactions](classify-transactions.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:121
msgid ""
"Use the invoice commands when you also need to track whether an invoice "
"exists separately from the bank movement. Received invoices are supplier "
"invoices you owe; issued invoices are customer invoices owed to you:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:129
msgid ""
"For the full invoice-record workflow, see [Attach invoices and receipts"
"](ledger-evidence.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:132
msgid "Review rows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:134
msgid ""
"List rows, narrow the list with filters, inspect one row, and read its "
"event history. The sequence imports the quarter and walks the read "
"commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:141
msgid ""
"For a broader review queue, use `ledger review` to inspect selected rows "
"and `ledger check` to report aggregate ledger anomalies across periods. "
"Both are local-only:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:149
msgid "Export rows for review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:151
msgid ""
"Export the active ledger to a file. The `--year` and `--period` filter "
"keeps the export aligned with the transaction dates. Exports are review "
"snapshots, not an edit-and-reimport path:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:159
msgid ""
"Add `--export-format xlsx` to write an XLSX snapshot instead, and use the"
" annual token `0A` when a whole year is the review scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:162
msgid ""
"To change saved rows, use `ledger update`, `ledger classify`, `ledger "
"allocate`, `ledger split`, or `ledger merge`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:165
msgid "Update a row"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:167
msgid ""
"Use `ledger update` for editable transaction fields - date, value date, "
"amount, direction, currency, counterparty, description, taxable base, IVA"
" rate, IVA amount, IRPF category, notes, or group label:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:175
msgid ""
"An update gives the transaction a new id; an id you wrote down earlier "
"still resolves in `view`, `history`, and `track`. For the full correction"
" workflow - splitting, merging, archiving, stashing, removing, and "
"resetting rows - see [Correct mistakes in your ledger](correct-ledger-"
"entries.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:180
msgid "Attach evidence to a transaction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:182
msgid ""
"Attach secure purchase evidence to a transaction. The evidence id comes "
"from `aeat app ledger evidence add`. The sequence records evidence and an"
" expense, then attaches one to the other:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:190
msgid ""
"`attach` is the single door for purchase evidence. The `link` command "
"binds a transaction to a reconciliation-catalogue invoice only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:193
msgid ""
"The `link --invoice-id` option expects an id from the reconciliation "
"invoice catalogue (populated by the import and reconcile flows), not an "
"id from `aeat app ledger invoice add`. See [Attach invoices and receipts"
"](ledger-evidence.md) for the full evidence and invoice-record workflow, "
"including the `--attachment-id` option and its current limitation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:200
msgid ""
"Pull a document straight from Google Drive into encrypted evidence "
"storage with `doclink`. This command reaches Google Drive, so it runs "
"against your own authorized account rather than in the documentation "
"sandbox:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:207
msgid ""
"The command downloads the Drive file, stores its bytes encrypted with the"
" transaction, and keeps the original link as provenance. Gmail links, "
"arbitrary URLs, and Drive files outside the granted scope are refused - "
"evidence always carries the document itself, never a bare link. For a "
"refused source, download the document yourself and attach it with `aeat "
"app ledger attach --attachment-id`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:214
msgid "Fix a wrong row"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:216
msgid ""
"Splitting a mixed movement into parts, merging a wrong split back, and "
"archiving, stashing, removing, or resetting rows are all corrections. "
"[Correct mistakes in your ledger](correct-ledger-entries.md) owns that "
"workflow, with an example for each command and guidance on picking the "
"least destructive fix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:222
msgid "Classify rows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:224
msgid ""
"Classify rows before calculation. At a minimum, imported business rows "
"need a business/personal/mixed decision, and expense rows need a "
"category:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:231
msgid ""
"[Classify transactions](classify-transactions.md) owns the full workflow "
"- bulk CSV classification, mixed-use allocation, tax fields, stored "
"rules, and [LLM-assisted suggestions](classify-with-llm.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:235
msgid "Check readiness for a filing period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:237
msgid ""
"Run preflight before calculating a modelo, then check the overall ledger "
"state. Preflight looks at each record inside the period and flags "
"anything still missing before any sums are trusted - a missing "
"classification, category, base, IVA amount, IVA rate, split reference, or"
" unconvertible currency:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:246
msgid ""
"The check changes nothing; it names the rows that are not ready so you "
"fix the raw material before trusting any total. Continue to calculation "
"only when the active profile and target period are ready enough for the "
"modelo you are preparing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:251
msgid ""
"For calculation review in Google Sheets, see [Review calculations with "
"Google Sheets](review-with-google-sheets.md). That workflow exports a "
"modelo calculation surface to Sheets; it is separate from ledger CSV/XLSX"
" export."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:256
msgid "If a command stops with an error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/import-bank-statements.md:258
msgid ""
"If a command reports that no profile is active, the period is invalid, or"
" the ledger is not ready, use [Diagnose and repair your local "
"setup](troubleshooting.md)."
msgstr ""

